WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
CMD ["python", "app.py"]

Here:
FROM sunil/mybase:v1
means: "Use sunil/mybase:v1 as the base image for my new image."
It doesn't matter whether the image is public or private. The FROM syntax is the same.
But Docker needs permission to pull it

Before building, login to Docker Hub:
docker login
Enter your Docker Hub username and password/token.
Now Docker knows: "This user is authenticated and can access private images."

4. Now build your image
docker build -t myapp:v1 .

Docker sees:
FROM sunil/mybase:v1
and tries to pull:
sunil/mybase:v1
Because you already did docker login, Docker can access the private image.

Simple difference
Image	docker login needed?	docker pull
Public	❌ No	✅ Yes
Private	✅ Yes	✅ Yes





